# Documentation Contract

Use this rule when changing onboarding docs, contributor policy docs, or
command references.

## Core Pattern

- Follow `AGENTS.md` "Documentation Contract" as the canonical policy.
- Keep `README.md` for technical onboarding and `CONTRIBUTING.md` for
  contributor policy.
- Keep command snippets synchronized with `package.json` and
  `docs/05-runbook-local.md`.
- Document scaffold placeholders explicitly (for example `/provider-status`
  with `actionable: false`).
- Keep dependency automation docs synchronized with `.github/dependabot.yml`,
  `pnpm-lock.yaml` expectations, and GitHub Dependabot alert behavior.
- Keep release-label guidance synchronized with `.github/release.yml` and
  `.github/workflows/pr-automation.yml`.

## Integration Points

- `README.md` is the internal technical entry point.
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` is the contributor policy source.
- `docs/05-runbook-local.md` is the local operational sequence.
- `apps/service/src/http/provider-status.ts` defines current provider status
  scaffold behavior.
- `package.json` is the command source of truth.
- `.github/dependabot.yml` owns dependency update scheduling.
- `.github/release.yml` owns generated release-note labels and exclusions.
- `.github/workflows/pr-automation.yml` owns automated PR type-label behavior.

## Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Preferred handling |
| --- | --- |
| Putting branch/release policy in `README.md` | Keep policy in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and link it |
| Declaring scaffold routes as complete | Mark placeholders explicitly and reference current behavior |
| Doc commands drifting from scripts | Validate every documented command against `package.json` |
| Treating `pnpm audit` as Dependabot closure proof | Use it only as an npm advisory cross-check; GitHub alert closure is confirmed after GitHub rescans |
| Documenting manual labels as automated | Distinguish PR automation type labels from manual labels such as `dependencies` |
| Writing non-runnable snippets | Keep command blocks copy-pasteable as-is |

